## memory-only change  (add memory: 12288, env unchanged)

$ docs/qa/ac-50k/install.sh trigger-v3-memory.yml
save 13:26:31.3   HTTP 201 version 4   latency 21.533 s      <-- see finding 3

after 6 s:
  machine bb340165 alive specs {"envHash":"329c4977…","memoryMb":12288,"npmPrefix":"…","bootstrapHash":"06a53e14…"}
  daemon  a86478c3 active connected 13:25:30.746 disconnected 13:25:26.443   (unchanged by this save)
  GET /v1/sprites/<n>/policy/resources -> {"memory":{"limit_mb":12288}}
  pgrep -f "paseo start --foreground"  -> 827  (unchanged: no restart)
  new Hub log lines: none — this path logs nothing

PASS on effect. The 21.5 s latency was chased down:

  sprite status at the time of the repeat runs: "warm"
  direct POST /v1/sprites/<n>/policy/resources {"memory":{"limit_mb":12288}}  -> 0.32 s, 0.35 s
  install.sh with memory: 10240  (warm)   -> latency 0.735 s, policy reads 10240
  install.sh with memory: 12288  (warm)   -> latency 0.364 s, policy reads 12288
  install.sh identical again     (warm)   -> latency 0.339 s

So a memory-only save is 0.34-0.74 s when the sprite is warm. The single 21.5 s sample was 26 s after the
last exec, when the sprite had probably been paused; Hub logs nothing on this path, so it is not attributable
from the evidence. Recorded as finding 3, not as a failure.

